From ca29bc16dc87615a3f644a022ab5fd0e4eaa111b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:13:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] Core: make FreeCADCmd behave like the Python executable
 when running scripts

- Run a .py file exactly once as __main__. It was imported as a module first
  and, if that raised, executed a second time, so failing scripts ran twice
  and 'if __name__ == "__main__":' blocks never ran.
- Exit with a non-zero code when a command line file fails or does not
  exist (was always 0), including --output export failures.
- Print the full Python traceback for script errors, not only the message.
- sys.exit() / sys.exit(None) exit with 0 (was 1); sys.exit("msg") prints
  the message to stderr.
- sys.argv is [script, args...] where args follow '--' or '--pass', so
  'FreeCADCmd script.py -- a b' works like 'python script.py a b'.
- Do not print the banner when running files non-interactively.
- Flush Python's stdout/stderr before exit() so output printed right
  before an error or sys.exit() is not lost.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
